message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "Techno-Economic Feasibility of a Decentralized Wind-UGES Microgrid in an Abandoned Mine Shaft"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible analysis code for the feasibility study of a 50 MW wind farm
  paired with a 5 MW Underground Gravity Energy Storage (UGES) retrofit in a
  494 m abandoned coal shaft at Jhimpir, Pakistan. Includes grid load flow,
  energy-management dispatch, shaft-foundation settlement, structural
  verification, wire-rope sizing, shaft-arrest and emergency-discharge design,
  strike survivability, and life-cycle embodied-carbon models.
type: software
